You reckon that's bad. I WON the game with a Valkyrie without seeing a
single shop. How annoying. Although I must admit that if you're going to
have a shopless game, a Valkyrie would have to be the easiest character
to play. Excellent weapon (Excalibur), good armor class and high hit
points make for a great hack and slash game.

Regarding shop probabilities, someone posted shop generation stuff a
while ago. It went something like this:

   A shop has a chance of being created if when a level is generated
   there is a room with only one entrance/exit with a door, and no
   stairs, traps, hidden doors, etc. If the door is locked the shop
   will be "closed for inventory".

   Once the possibility of a shop exists, then the chances on each level
   of a shop being created are:
                                Level       Percentage Chance
				  1                0 %
                                 2,3              100 %
				 4+          (1 / level no.) %

This is all from memory and second hand, so some of it may be wrong.
As you can see, to actually calculate a probability would be very
difficult.

